<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<pythonPanelDocument>
  <!-- Installed by install.py, which injects this repo's path into the script
 below so the panel imports parmesan without any environment setup. -->
  <interface name="parmesan" label="Parmesan" icon="MISC_python" help_url="">
    <script><![CDATA[
# PARMESAN_PATH_INJECTION

def onCreateInterface():
    import importlib
    import parmesan.panel

    # Reload on every open so editing a source file and reopening the panel
    # shows the change, instead of needing a Houdini restart.
    importlib.reload(parmesan.panel)
    return parmesan.panel.create()
]]></script>
    <includeInPaneTabMenu menu_position="300" create_separator="false"/>
    <includeInToolbarMenu menu_position="300" create_separator="false"/>
    <help><![CDATA[
Parmesan surfaces the parameters that matter from a whole Houdini graph onto
one control node, without taking the graph hostage.

1. Select a node and press Create New to make a CONTROLS null.
2. Press Scan Graph and Build Panel. Every node under the scan root is read,
   every parameter ranked, and the best ones surfaced - grouped into one
   folder per source node.
3. Press Show Controls to bring the sliders up in the Parameters pane. That
   is where the controls live; this panel is the machinery around them.
4. Press Refresh after changing something in the graph directly. The button
   shows how many things need attention.

The graph stays master: node parms own every value, and removing a control
never changes anything in the graph.
]]></help>
  </interface>
</pythonPanelDocument>
